        "original_id": "d15004bd-b7cd-55d2-99a1-0bbdf2ff091d",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Konstantin Somov, Andrey Ivanovich Somov, Alexandre Benois, Léon Bakst, Walter Nouvel, Dmitry Filosofov\n- Organizations: Hermitage Museum, Nevsky Pickwickians\n- Roles: art historian, curator, leader\n- Concepts: 18th-century art, music\n\nFacts:\n- The Hermitage Museum has been open to the public since 1852.\n- Konstantin Somov was born into a family of major art historian and Hermitage Museum curator Andrey Ivanovich Somov.\n- Konstantin Somov became interested in 18th-century art and music at an early age.\n- The Nevsky Pickwickians originally included Alexandre Benois, Léon Bakst, Walter Nouvel, Dmitry Filosofov, and Konstantin Somov.\n- Alexandre Benois was effectively the leader of the Nevsky Pickwickians.",
